From 6bbc7559428503cb1d937c80d768b50338451752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:49:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: qcom_smd: Drop the retained edge node on release

qcom_smd_parse_edge() retains the edge device-tree node with of_node_get().
Error paths drop that reference and clear edge->of_node, but successful
registration never releases it when the edge is removed. Repeated successful
registration/removal therefore leaves another node reference behind. The
reference is also retained when a later registration step fails.

Release the saved reference in qcom_smd_edge_release(), after the channels
are freed. A NULL edge->of_node from an earlier parse failure is harmless.
The device core does not release this separately retained driver reference.

A host model executes the actual parse, register, child removal, unregister
and release bodies with synthetic OF/device/mailbox/IRQ/work services. It
reproduces 16 reference imbalances before this change; all 81 cases pass
with it, including mailbox and syscon paths, failure boundaries, and the
local noirq-capable RPM draft. Six clean assertion controls reject broken
reference, IRQ, notifier and work cleanup. These are synthetic host checks,
not physical device or kernel concurrency qualification.

Native ARM and ARM64 ordinary/RT builds pass with no new diagnostics. The
two pre-existing RPMsg kernel-doc warnings per profile are retained.
Public source history verifies the original unmatched node acquisition.

Codex found the issue and generated the fix, host tests and this draft
message during the Fx0 bringup audit. Human review and DCO remain pending.
Nothing has been submitted.

Fixes: 53e2822e56c7 ("rpmsg: Introduce Qualcomm SMD backend")

Maintainer-base validation is recorded separately from the original
integration lifecycle models. This local replay preserves the source
change and attribution; human review and DCO are still pending.

(cherry picked from commit 65fcce0588a4e70325c16834954b76ee914f418b)
---
 drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c
index 7dbe1c6ef..7cfde3dea 100644
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c
@@ -1452,6 +1452,7 @@ static void qcom_smd_edge_release(struct device *dev)
 		kfree(channel);
 	}
 
+	of_node_put(edge->of_node);
 	kfree(edge);
 }
 
